{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Put no [D]stone at my head, No [G]flowers on my tomb
No [D]gold plated sign In a [A]marbled pillared room
The [D]one thing I want, When they [G]lay me in the ground
When I [D]die, [A]Tear my stillhouse [D]down
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Oh, [G]Tear my stillhouse down, Let it go to rust
Don't [D]leave no trace of the hiding place, Where I made that evil stuff
For [G]all my time and money, No profit did I see
That [D]old copper kettle was the [A]death of [D]me
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
When I was a child, Way back in the hills
I laughed at the men, Who tended those stills
But that old mountain shine, It caught me somehow
When I die, Tear my stillhouse down
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
Oh, Tell all your children, That Hell ain't no dream
'Cause Satan he lives, In my whiskey machine
And in my time of dying I know where I'm bound
When I die, Tear my stillhouse down
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_chorus}
Chorus a second time as instrumental
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
That [D]old copper kettle was the [A]death of [D]me
{end_of_verse}
